        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sgs" value="&lt;b&gt;Security groups&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;rafael-forestproject-db-sg&lt;/b&gt; — in: TCP 5432 &lt;b&gt;only from the EKS cluster security group&lt;/b&gt; (SG-to-SG reference; before: EKS subnet CIDRs) · no egress rule&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;EKS cluster SG&lt;/b&gt; — created by EKS: node↔node, control plane ↔ nodes · out via NAT&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;NLB&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font color='#C2410C'&gt;&lt;b&gt;PLANNED&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; — in: TCP 80 (443 once TLS is added) from 0.0.0.0/0 · SG created by Kubernetes&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;EKS API&lt;/b&gt; — public endpoint limited to your IP /32 (tested: other networks time out)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#F8F9FA;strokeColor=#AAB7B8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#232F3E;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="680" y="1460" width="700" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Azure → AWS: AKS → EKS, ACR → ECR, Key Vault → Secrets Manager (+ CSI + Pod Identity), Postgres Flexible → RDS PostgreSQL, NSGs → security groups.&lt;br&gt;• HA: NAT per AZ, Multi-AZ RDS, one node per AZ. S3 gateway endpoint cuts NAT data costs for ECR pulls.&lt;br&gt;• Next: build + push the app image to ECR, K8s manifests (ServiceAccount, SecretProviderClass provider: aws), then GitHub Actions with OIDC.&lt;br&gt;• Lab: ~$0.35/hr while applied → terraform destroy after each session." style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fillColor=#F8F9FA;strokeColor=#AAB7B8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#232F3E;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1400" y="1460" width="520" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
